.SH NAME
Plack::Session::Store::File \- Basic file\-based session store
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 3
\&  use Plack::Builder;
\&  use Plack::Middleware::Session;
\&  use Plack::Session::Store::File;
\&
\&  my $app = sub {
\&      return [ 200, [ \*(AqContent\-Type\*(Aq => \*(Aqtext/plain\*(Aq ], [ \*(AqHello Foo\*(Aq ] ];
\&  };
\&
\&  builder {
\&      enable \*(AqSession\*(Aq,
\&          store => Plack::Session::Store::File\->new(
\&              dir => \*(Aq/path/to/sessions\*(Aq
\&          );
\&      $app;
\&  };
\&
\&  # with custom serializer/deserializer
\&
\&  builder {
\&      enable \*(AqSession\*(Aq,
\&          store => Plack::Session::Store::File\->new(
\&              dir          => \*(Aq/path/to/sessions\*(Aq,
\&              # YAML takes it\*(Aqs args the opposite order
\&              serializer   => sub { YAML::DumpFile( reverse @_ ) },
\&              deserializer => sub { YAML::LoadFile( @_ ) },
\&          );
\&      $app;
\&  };
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
This implements a basic file based storage for session data. By
default it will use Storable to serialize and deserialize the
data, but this can be configured easily.
.PP
This is a subclass of Plack::Session::Store and implements
its full interface.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.ie n .IP "\fBnew ( \fR\fB%params\fR\fB )\fR" 4
.el .IP "\fBnew ( \fR\f(CB%params\fR\fB )\fR" 4
.IX Item "new ( %params )"
The \f(CW%params\fR can include \fIdir\fR, \fIserializer\fR and \fIdeserializer\fR
options. It will check to be sure that the \fIdir\fR is writeable for
you.
.IP \fBdir\fR 4
.IX Item "dir"
This is the directory to store the session data files in, if nothing
is provided then File::Spec's \fBtmpdir()\fR is used to determine the
system's temp dir.
.IP \fBserializer\fR 4
.IX Item "serializer"
This is a CODE reference that implements the serialization logic.
The CODE ref gets two arguments, the \f(CW$value\fR, which is a HASH
reference to be serialized, and the \f(CW$file_path\fR to save it to.
It is not expected to return anything.
.IP \fBdeserializer\fR 4
.IX Item "deserializer"
This is a CODE reference that implements the deserialization logic.
The CODE ref gets one argument, the \f(CW$file_path\fR to load the data
from. It is expected to return a HASH reference.
